                <pb facs="0457" n="397" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg397"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr. Eustis</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-02-11"><hi rendition="#italic">February 11,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Instruction mailed you to-day concerning apprehended demonstration of French
                    Government against Santo Domingo and possible impairment of rights of American
                    citizens as farmers of Santo Domingo customs revenue under contract. It is
                    reported a cabinet meeting will be held Paris to-morrow (Tuesday) to determine
                    action against Santo Domingo. Notify minister for foreign affairs of existing
                    rights of American citizens, in order that they may be duly protected in any
                    action France may take for enforcement of her claim.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gresham</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
